			<span class="elementor-divider-separator">
						</span>
		</div>
						</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-e2f9d4e elementor-widget elementor-widget-theme-post-content" data-id="e2f9d4e" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="theme-post-content.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The board of directors have no authority to set values or appraisal methods. Its required duties and authority are prescribed by the Texas Property Tax Code, and include&nbsp;establishing the appraisal district office,&nbsp;hiring a Chief Appraiser,&nbsp;appointing the Taxpayer Liaison Officer,&nbsp;appointing the Appraisal Review Board,&nbsp;adopting the district’s biennial reappraisal plan,&nbsp;and&nbsp;adopting the district’s annual operating budget.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Directors on the Collin Central Appraisal District&#8217;s Board of Directors</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Richard Grady (Chairman)</li>



<li>Randal Shinn (Secretary) &#8211; Place 1</li>



<li>Scott Grigg – Tax Assessor/Collector</li>



<li>Doug Bender</li>



<li>Alvin Benton</li>



<li>Jason Ross</li>



<li>Veronica Yost</li>



<li>Sumbel Zeb – Place 2</li>



<li>Andrew Cook – Place 3</li>
</ul>



<div style="height:36px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://collincad.org/category/miscellaneous-downloads/board-of-directors/board-of-directors-meeting-agenda-packets/">Click here</a>&nbsp;for the latest&nbsp;BOD&nbsp;agenda packets.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://collincad.org/category/miscellaneous-downloads/board-of-directors/">Click here</a>&nbsp;to see the Board of Directors&#8217; Policies.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://collincad.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/2025-2026_Collin_CAD_Reappraisal_Plan.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Click here</a>&nbsp;for the adopted 2025-2026 Reappraisal Plan.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://waitwhile.com/locations/bod" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Click here</a> if you will be attending an up-coming Board of Directors meeting and check-in as a guest by filling out the form.&nbsp; Scheduled board meetings start at 6pm, public comments are held at the beginning of the meeting and reserved for those who <a href="https://waitwhile.com/locations/bod" target="_blank" rel="noopener">check-in</a>.&nbsp; Each public speaker is allotted 5 minutes unless the Board extends time.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">All correspondence to the Board of Directors should be directed to: 250 Eldorado PKWY, McKinney, Texas 75069 or BoardOfDirectors@collincad.org.<br></p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The 88th Texas Legislature passed new legislation for counties with a population of 75,000 or more, calling for three members of the appraisal district board of directors to be elected by the public at a general election for At-Large Place 1, At-Large Place 2 and At-Large Place 3. Please see the links below for additional election information and for further questions, please <a href="https://www.collincountytx.gov/elections">contact the Collin County Election Office</a>:</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8211;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.sos.state.tx.us/elections/laws/running-for-county-appraisal-districts-2026.shtml">Texas Secretary of State &#8211; Running for County Appraisal Districts</a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.collincountytx.gov/Elections/notices">Collin County Election Office Notices</a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://collincad.org/wp-content/uploads/Collin-Central-Appraisal-District-Notice-of-Drawing-for-a-Place-on-Ballot-8.26.2026.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Notice of drawing for a place on ballot 2026-11-03</a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8211;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
		</div>
